INT. GENERATION SHIP "MERIDIAN" - SEED VAULT - SHIP'S NIGHT

A frozen cavern of steel drawers, floor to ceiling. Blue frost on the rails. Breath fogs in the air.

Five crew in thermal suits, headlamps swinging, work a cart down the center aisle.

CAPTAIN IFEOMA ROTHSCHILD-ADAMU, 50s, leads. CHIEF BOTANIST HAKON LEIVESTAD, 40s, carries a scanner. ENGINEER PRAVEEN MBANDAKA-DOYLE, 30s, hauls a toolbox. TECHNICIAN SOLENNE ACHTERBERG-NGO, 20s, monitors a wrist display. And YUSUF KAZEMI-BROOKS, 30s, medic, trails with a field kit.

IFEOMA
(to all)
Vault Four. Be quick. The air scrubbers fail in nine minutes.

HAKON
Drawer four-twelve.

PRAVEEN
(muttering)
Four-twelve, four-twelve.

SOLENNE
Temperature's rising.

YUSUF
How much?

SOLENNE
Two degrees. In a minute.

IFEOMA
Move.

They reach the drawer. Hakon scans. Green light. He pulls. Inside: row upon row of tiny vials, frosted white.

HAKON
(softly)
The wheat.

PRAVEEN
Take it.

HAKON
All of it.

He lifts a rack. Hands it to Solenne. She slides it into a cooler. Yusuf hovers, anxious.

The ship shudders. A klaxon begins, low and pulsing.

IFEOMA
(to Solenne)
Status.

SOLENNE
Cooling's gone on Deck Nine. Six minutes.

IFEOMA
Understood.

At the far end of the aisle, a hatch slides open. A figure steps through, silhouetted by red emergency light.

COMMANDER DEWITT LARKSPUR-OSEI, 60s, black uniform, a sidearm drawn, stands in the doorway.

LARKSPUR
Nobody touches the seed.

The five crew freeze. Hakon, mid-lift, half-turns. Praveen's toolbox hits the floor. Solenne steps back. Yusuf raises both hands. Ifeoma does not move.

IFEOMA
Commander. The vault is failing.

LARKSPUR
The vault is mine.

IFEOMA
The ship will starve.

LARKSPUR
The ship will obey.

A tense silence. The klaxon pulses.

SOLENNE
(whispering)
Captain...

IFEOMA
(low)
Easy.

HAKON
(to himself)
The wheat is warming.

Ifeoma takes one slow step forward, palms open.

IFEOMA
Dewitt. We both took the oath.

LARKSPUR
I took it first.

He steps closer. The gun trembles.

IFEOMA
Then keep it. Open the lock. Let us take the seed.

A beat. Then Larkspur lowers his weapon. Hand shaking, he pulls a keycard from his jacket and sweeps it over the panel. A deep thunk. The vault door opens wider.

LARKSPUR
(hoarse)
Go.

They run. The cart rattles. Frost sprays from the wheels. Behind them, the Commander stays by the hatch, watching them vanish into the dark with the ship's future in a cooler.
